# winemac: Update the GL context directly when already on the main thread.
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/12371 state=opened
# I found the bug while trying to play Halo 3 reclaimer mod, the screen just froze on launch, so I did a deep dive.

macdrv_update_opengl_context() is reached from \[WineContentView viewWillDraw\] on the main thread when a context was still pending at the time the view became visible. The "update" branch then calls OnMainThread(), which queues the block for the main run loop and waits on a semaphore forever behind its own wait, since the main thread is the one waiting. and therefore we have a deadlock.

The window stops being serviced (I got a spinning cursor) and every Wine thread that needs the main thread hangs with it.

Observed with an application that attaches an OpenGL context to a window already hosting a Metal-backed (D3DMetal) swap chain.

I derived the pattern here from the two other OnMainThread() call sites in this file already guard with -\[NSThread isMainThread\]. So I did the same here and it worked.
--- dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_opengl.m
+++ dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_opengl.m
@@ -308,6 +308,8 @@ void macdrv_update_opengl_context(WineOpenGLContext *context)
                 [context clearDrawableLeavingSurfaceOnScreen];
                 context.view = view;
             }
+            else if ([NSThread isMainThread])
+                [context update];
             else OnMainThread(^{
                 [context update];
             });

